  "part_lines": [
    "\\monographpart{Polyhedra and moduli measures}{Polyhedral realization supplies coordinates; the measure comparison turns them into volume formulas. Fixed-deficit Euclidean shapes then reveal a period geometry at the flat limit.}\n",
    "\\monographpart{Variational geometry and computation}{The volume Hessian becomes a discrete Dirichlet operator. Boundary elimination, Gaussian determinants, and barrier methods connect the geometry to computation.}\n",
    "\\monographpart{Quantum geometry, degeneration, and surgery}{An introduction to the quantum constructions leads to exact period comparisons, a controlled tetrahedral degeneration, and the classical and Gaussian data of Dehn filling.}\n",
    "\\monographpart{Curves, trace formulas, and quotients}{Cutting and gluing geodesics produces identities and twist integrals. Twisted trace formulas retain the multicurve coefficients and their lengths.}\n",
    "\\monographpart{Mapping-class dynamics and mixing}{Weighted endpoint counts encode correlations. The general converse specifies the required estimates, while the marked-torus model supplies an explicit calculation on one genus-two stratum.}\n",
    "\\monographpart{Sharp counting and arithmetic}{The local shape of a norm ball governs geometric discrepancy. Primitive counting adds a separate arithmetic cancellation problem, and exact diagnostics keep the two inputs visible.}\n",
    "\\monographpart{Open problems and conjectural directions}{The comparisons suggest concrete further estimates, integrations, and gluing problems. Their hypotheses identify what the next results would need to establish.}\n"
